# Port patch, the cheat "Stack items" for more items (1.1.3, the project owner: grenades of all kinds, herbs of all kinds
# and their mixes, first aid sprays, fish and eggs as well; not weapons, treasures or key items). Patch 0254 made the ammo
# stack; here itemInfo asks runtime/cheats.cpp re4_stack_kind (ammo, recovery items = type 6, the grenades 0x01, 0x02,
# 0x0E; type 3 also holds the rocket launchers, which stay one a slot).
# - The case (ss_pzzl.cpp) shows a count where the game does, and on a stack of an item the game keeps one a slot (a
#   grenade, a herb) only when there is more than one: no "1" on a single grenade (re4_item_game_max: the game's limit).
# - Mixing a herb taken from a stack (cItemMgr::combine, the type 6 arm): the game takes one of each and gets the mix as a
#   new slot; with a stack left there the new slot had no place in the case. The case screen's two combines (the Combine
#   command, PieceCombine; a piece in the hand put on another, pzlPlayer::cmbPiece) open a Re4StackCase, and
#   re4_stack_combined puts the mix onto a stack of that mix with room, else into a free place of the case (upright,
#   then turned, as PutInCase does); no room: the combine is undone (nothing mixed, nothing lost, the game's "can't" sound). The screen builds the new piece's model
#   (re4_stack_case_placed). A single herb mixed as before (the mix takes its place).
# - A stack above the item's limit (the cheat switched off, or a lower value chosen): PutInCase counted it as room of
#   max - num (negative, or a wrap-around in u16) and its fill loop set it down to the limit (the rest of the stack was
#   lost; with ammo since 1.1.0); now it has no room and keeps its count, a pick-up goes to the other stacks or a new
#   slot. Combining two ammo or grenade stacks onto such a stack takes nothing (cItemMgr::combine, room <= 0).
# Off (Standard): as the game, but for the two room fixes, which only matter for such a stack.
